    "why": "The three major chords of a key are built on its 1st, 4th and 5th notes, and on the circle of fifths they sit side by side, so the circle finds them in any key.",
    "learnBefore": [
      "/course/5/one-four-five",
      "/course/10/circle-map"
    ],
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "section",
        "heading": "Three neighbours",
        "minutes": 3,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The circle below is on C major, and the keys marked on its outer ring are F, C and G: the 4, the 1 and the 5 of the key. Tap F to hear its chord: the circle moves there, so tap C to come back. Do the same with G."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "circle-of-fifths",
              "key": "c",
              "scale": "major-ionian"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On the staff below, tap the three ringed notes, {{1}}, {{4}} and {{5}}: each one is the root of one of those chords."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "staff",
              "scale": "major-ionian",
              "key": "c",
              "voice": "tenor",
              "highlight": [
                "1",
                "4",
                "5"
              ],
              "mic": false
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "section",
        "heading": "Follow the backing track",
        "minutes": 2,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press Play below to start the backing track: C, F, G and back to C, one bar each. Call out 1, 4 or 5 as each chord arrives, with the chord boxes to help.\nKeep going until you hear a change coming before the box lights."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "backing-track",
              "key": "c",
              "numerals": [
                "I",
                "IV",
                "V",
                "I"
              ],
              "style": "pop",
              "bpm": 80
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "section",
        "heading": "Guess from the circle",
        "minutes": 2,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The circle below is on G major. Read its 1, 4 and 5 off the marked keys on the outer ring before you listen."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "circle-of-fifths",
              "key": "g",
              "scale": "major-ionian"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press Play below to start the backing track in G: the same three numbers in a new order. Look away and call them out, then look back at the chord boxes to check.\nThe key is new, so the chords are G, C and D, but each number keeps its sound."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
